# Everything in this repo is consumed on Linux (GitHub Actions runners, and the
# Caddy/xray hosts). A CRLF anywhere breaks two things outright: bash scripts
# fail with "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M", and `git apply` rejects the
# patch because the context lines no longer match a LF working tree. Pin LF for
# every text file and never let the client's core.autocrlf rewrite it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Patch files must be byte-identical to their upstream origin, so they are
# excluded from any normalisation whatsoever.
*.patch -text
*.diff  -text

# Binary-ish assets stay binary.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.zip binary
*.xz  binary
